# Template only -- lists the variable names this stack's docker-compose.yml
# expects. Real values live in Infisical, never here and never in git.
# scripts/render-env.sh writes the actual .env next to this file on the host.
#
# FileBrowser doesn't use any ${VAR} substitution in its docker-compose.yml
# either -- there's nothing to fill in here. Its container runs as a fixed
# user (user: "1000:1000", hardcoded rather than pulled from PUID/PGID) and
# is only reachable directly on host port 8085 today rather than through
# Traefik (no Traefik labels are defined for it in the compose file), so
# there's no INTERNAL_DOMAIN-style hostname var either. Whatever config
# FileBrowser itself needs (users, permissions, branding) lives in its own
# ./database.db, edited through its web UI, not through env vars.
